{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791139571,"nonce":"P3Qjdm4vQESJqoLFMvOH9o8U/g4=","title":"a macOS poll takes in nothing the window server sends","message":"Since e505c4a3afd470c814973a267e2b8dc5b0982799 a poll on macOS posts its stop event behind the queued events and stops on it. -[NSApplication run] dequeues queued events without a run-loop pass, so a program that only polls never gets the window server's events. Reported by ashui-8b: with hlwindow e6b2fca, ashui's wgpu surface never yielded a texture.\n\nReproducer: a wgpu loop that polls and presents (pollbench src/bin/wgpu.rs, POLLONLY=1, 4 s):\n  8d581e7: 463 frames, 2 refused, 10 events\n  e505c4a: 0 frames, 74349 refused, 0 events\nA raw CAMetalLayer loop (present through a command buffer) presented fine on e505c4a, so the failure goes through wgpu's surface. The missing window-server events are the likely cause.\n\nashui-8b's pin went back to 8d581e7 (hlwindow fa8617b) meanwhile.","files":null}]}